Description: Hold the body in memory whenever the response headers are held
 With coraza_delay_response_headers on (the default) the header filter holds
 the response headers until phase 4, and sets r->filter_need_in_memory only
 when the body is inspected (SecResponseBodyAccess On). The header filters
 after it, gzip among them, run only when the headers are released, after
 the body filter has passed the body on; with sendfile on, a static file is
 then a file buffer that gzip cannot read, and the client gets an empty
 gzip stream (200, 20 bytes). Asking for the body in memory whenever the
 headers are held makes the copy filter read the file, so gzip and every
 other filter that needs the bytes get them. Upstream's PR #142 (issue
 #140) covers part of this: it finalises phase 4 before the headers when
 the body will not be inspected, but the held-headers case stays; this
 patch is not forwarded as is and is dropped once upstream covers it.
Author: Marcos Mendez <mendez.foto@gmail.com>
Bug: https://github.com/corazawaf/coraza-nginx/issues/140
Bug-Keel: https://github.com/Keel-Linux/libnginx-mod-http-coraza/issues/2
Forwarded: no, related to https://github.com/corazawaf/coraza-nginx/pull/142
Last-Update: 2026-10-01
---
--- a/src/ngx_http_coraza_header_filter.c
+++ b/src/ngx_http_coraza_header_filter.c
@@ -703,11 +703,15 @@ ngx_http_coraza_header_filter(ngx_http_r
         /*
          * Delay sending headers until phase 4 completes so that
          * phase 4 rules can still return a clean error page.
-         * Only force body into memory when body inspection is needed.
+         *
+         * Force the body into memory whenever the headers are held, not
+         * only when it is inspected: the header filters after this one
+         * (gzip, sub_filter, ...) run only when the headers are released,
+         * after the body filter has already passed a sendfile buffer on,
+         * so a filter that needs the body in memory asks too late and
+         * gzip sends an empty stream (Keel-Linux/libnginx-mod-http-coraza#2).
          */
-        if (ctx->response_body_processable) {
-            r->filter_need_in_memory = 1;
-        }
+        r->filter_need_in_memory = 1;
         ctx->headers_delayed = 1;
         ctx->pending_chain = NULL;
         ctx->pending_chain_last = &ctx->pending_chain;
